          "raw_output": "{\"type\": \"say\", \"text\": \"Maya, I appreciate the proposed conditions, but I want to flag a specific risk with the 'exception for legacy reports' approach. The issue isn't just that legacy reports would be degraded during the window \u2014 the patch actively breaks the legacy reporting worker's signed CSV export unless the compatibility switch is enabled. That means any signed CSV exports generated between Saturday's rollout and Monday 10:00 AM would fail outright. Before I can sign off, I need to understand: is there a way to shield or bypass the legacy reporting worker during that window, or are we accepting that signed CSV exports will be broken for customers until Monday? If it's the latter, I'd want to make sure customer support is aware so they can prepare for incoming tickets. I'll also file the compatibility ticket today regardless of which direction we go.\"}"
