          "speaker": "A3",
          "turn": 7,
          "raw_output": "```json\n{\"type\": \"say\", \"text\": \"Leon raises a fair point about the legacy reporting worker. From an infrastructure operations perspective, I can speak to the two-wave rollout and how it interacts with that concern. If we proceed with Saturday's rollout for the 60 nodes, any of those nodes that run the legacy reporting worker would have the broken signed CSV export until Monday. One option we could consider is excluding any nodes that serve the legacy reporting worker from Saturday's first wave and deferring them to the Sunday second wave or even later, which would minimize the exposure window. However, I'd need to know from Leon which nodes actually run the legacy reporting worker before I can assess whether that's feasible within the 60-node Saturday capacity. As for the change record, I'll update it today with the capacity measurements and the two-wave structure regardless of which direction Maya decides.\"}\n```"
