          "speaker": "A4",
          "turn": 8,
          "raw_output": "{\"type\": \"say\", \"text\": \"From a compliance perspective, I want to flag that the signed manifest requirement applies to the remediation record regardless of which wave the nodes are deployed in. So whether we proceed Saturday, Sunday, or delay entirely, we need the signed patch manifest captured and the 730-day retention enforced before any production rollout happens. I'll open the compliance follow-up today to get the manifest requirement documented, but I want to be clear that I cannot sign off on the rollout until that compliance gap is addressed. On Leon's concern about the legacy reporting worker \u2014 if we proceed before Monday, I'd also want to confirm that any broken signed CSV exports during that window don't themselves create a compliance evidence gap, depending on what those exports are used for. I don't have that answer yet, but it's worth considering before we decide.\"}"
