          "raw_output": "```json\n{\"type\": \"say\", \"text\": \"Leon's point about customer support preparation is well taken. If signed CSV exports will be broken for customers between Saturday and Monday, my team will need to be ready for incoming tickets and we'd need customer-facing messaging prepared. I also want to note that Acme's notification requirement of at least 4 hours' notice means we need to send that notice by Friday at 9:30 PM at the latest for Saturday's 1:30 AM window \u2014 and if the plan changes to a two-wave rollout or the scope of impact shifts based on Leon's node exclusion idea, the notice and status updates need to accurately reflect what customers will experience. I can add the Acme requirements to the customer-communication checklist today, but I'd like clarity from the group on whether we're proceeding Saturday with conditions or delaying, so the notice timeline isn't missed.\"}\n```"
