          "text": "Thank you all for the thorough discussion. I'm hearing several interlocking concerns that need to be resolved before I can make a final decision. Let me lay out what I see as the key decision points.\n\nFirst, on Leon's concern: the patch actively breaks signed CSV exports, not just degrades them. Nia's suggestion to exclude legacy reporting worker nodes from Saturday's first wave is promising, but we need Leon to identify which nodes those are before we can assess feasibility. Leon, can you provide that node list today so Nia can evaluate whether excluding them still leaves us with a viable Saturday wave?\n\nSecond, Owen has made clear he cannot sign off until the signed manifest with 730-day retention is in place, and that applies regardless of timing. Owen, can you confirm whether the compliance follow-up you're opening today can be resolved before Saturday, or does that itself push us past the weekend?\n\nThird, Owen also raised the question of whether broken signed CSV exports themselves create a compliance evidence gap. We need that answer before deciding to proceed.\n\nFourth, Tara's timeline is concrete: Acme needs notice by Friday 9:30 PM for a Saturday 1:30 AM window. If we can't resolve the compliance sign-off, the node exclusion question, and the compliance-evidence-gap question before then, we either miss that notice window or we delay.\n\nGiven all of this, I'm not prepared to approve the Saturday rollout right now. There are too many unresolved dependencies. I'd like to set a deadline: if we can get Leon's node list, Owen's compliance timeline, and Owen's assessment of the CSV export compliance gap by end of day today, we can reconvene and make a final call with enough time to notify Acme by Friday 9:30 PM. If any of those items can't be resolved today, we delay to Monday or later. Does that approach work for everyone?",
