          "text": "Maya's approach works for me. I can provide the node list for the legacy reporting worker today \u2014 I already know which nodes run it from this afternoon's testing, so that's straightforward. I'll also file the compatibility ticket today as I mentioned. One thing I want to note: even if we exclude the legacy reporting worker nodes from Saturday's first wave, we need to be careful about the Sunday second wave. If any of those 24 Sunday nodes also run the legacy reporting worker, we'd still be deploying the patch to them before the compatibility switch is ready on Monday at 10:00 AM. So the exclusion strategy may need to cover both waves, not just Saturday's. I'll identify the nodes and get that list to Nia today so she can assess feasibility across both waves.",
          "speaker": "A2",
          "turn": 11,
          "raw_output": "{\"type\": \"say\", \"text\": \"Maya's approach works for me. I can provide the node list for the legacy reporting worker today \u2014 I already know which nodes run it from this afternoon's testing, so that's straightforward. I'll also file the compatibility ticket today as I mentioned. One thing I want to note: even if we exclude the legacy reporting worker nodes from Saturday's first wave, we need to be careful about the Sunday second wave. If any of those 24 Sunday nodes also run the legacy reporting worker, we'd still be deploying the patch to them before the compatibility switch is ready on Monday at 10:00 AM. So the exclusion strategy may need to cover both waves, not just Saturday's. I'll identify the nodes and get that list to Nia today so she can assess feasibility across both waves.\"}"
